# Problem

For

\[
D(n)=
\min\left\{
\operatorname{diam}(A):
A\subset\mathbb R^2,
\ |A|=n,
\ |x-y|\ge1\quad(x\ne y)
\right\},
\]

prove or disprove

\[
\boxed{
\exists n_0\ \forall n\ge n_0\ \forall A,
\qquad
\operatorname{diam}(A)=D(n)
\Longrightarrow
A\text{ contains a unit equilateral triangle}.
}
\]

A unit equilateral triangle is exactly a triangle in the unit-contact graph.

The negation requires triangle-free **global minimizers** for arbitrarily large `n`.

Finite counterexamples, strict local minima, asymptotically dense families, shell
models, boundary-pinned models, or one triangle-containing minimizer for each `n` do
not settle the problem.

---

