# Global constants and exact shell gate

Use

\[
a_0=\frac{\sqrt3}{2},
\qquad
c_0=\frac{\sqrt3}{4},
\qquad
c=\frac{2\sqrt3}{\pi},
\qquad
C_0=\sqrt{2\pi\sqrt3}.
\]

The audited translated-lattice theorem is

\[
\boxed{D(n)^2<c(n-1).}
\]

For a topology-corrected rhombic core,

\[
\boxed{
 c_0(B-P)+a_0(t+\chi-1)
 \le G_{\mathcal R}+E_{\mathcal R}
 <c_0B+a_0(t+\chi-1).
}
\]

For a pure rhombic disk,

\[
\boxed{c_0(B-P)\le G+E<c_0B.}
\]

Thus the exact pure contradiction threshold is

\[
\boxed{G+E\ge c_0B.}
\]

There is no residual `+a0` term.

