# Target A normal form: all forest kinematics are finished

The rooted quotient forest satisfies

\[
\boxed{
\ell=u-r+c+\sigma,
\qquad
0\le\sigma\le r-c,
}
\]

so

\[
\ell=u-O(D).
\]

Root-skeleton exactification and forest rattlerization give a nearby triangle-free
global minimizer with strict-rattler set \(\mathscr R\) satisfying

\[
\boxed{
\rho:=|\mathscr R|
\ge u-r+c
\ge\ell-(r-c)
\ge\ell-\pi D.
}
\]

Each retained strict rattler has no unit contact, no active diameter incidence, and
strict slack in every constraint involving it.

The local same-`D` minimizer set contains an open product ball of dimension at least

\[
\boxed{2\rho\ge2\ell-2\pi D.}
\]

Do not work on forest rigidity, bar self-stress, generic hinge regularity, or isolated
triangle walls. Those are no longer the Target A obstruction.

