# Target A saturation

Any triangle-free global minimizer can be enlarged inside its fixed convex hull to a
triangle-free global minimizer of the same diameter by adding fewer than

\[
\boxed{\frac\pi2D}
\]

points, so that the fixed hull is unit-covered:

\[
K\subseteq\bigcup_{p\in A}\overline B(p,1).
\]

The retained strict rattlers can be kept non-diametral by generic insertion.

Thus a super-boundary Target A survivor may be assumed simultaneously:

- globally optimal;
- triangle-free;
- fixed diameter `D`;
- unit-covering saturated in its hull; and
- carrying \(\rho=\omega(D)\) genuine strict rattlers.

