# Target A: exact scaffold conflict graph

Let

\[
L=\operatorname{int}(K_m+t\mathbb B),
\qquad
Y=(\Lambda+v)\cap L,
\]

using the same lattice translate that gives the safe-collar count.

Build a bipartite conflict graph between \(X_m\) and `Y`, with

\[
x\sim y
\iff
|x-y|<1.
\]

Let \(\nu\) be its maximum matching size. The exact Hall--Kőnig theorem is

\[
\boxed{
m+|Y|-\nu\le N-1.}
\]

Equivalently, for every \(S\subseteq Y\),

\[
\boxed{|S|-|N(S)|\le\rho-1.}
\]

Let

\[
Y_0=Y\cap\Omega,
\qquad
|Y_0|=k,
\qquad
Y_{\rm in}=Y\setminus Y_0.
\]

Since `Y_0` has no conflicts with \(X_m\), every \(Q\subseteq Y_{\rm in}\) satisfies

\[
\boxed{
|Q|-|N(Q)|\le\rho-k-1=j-1.
}
\]

Hence the inner-band conflict graph has a matching into \(X_m\) leaving at most
`j-1=O(D)` inner-band lattice sites unmatched.

This is a matching of **conflicts**. It is not the desired grafting.

